MID_EV00_012_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV00_012_m01_001: And here we are.
MID_EV00_012_m01_002: It's strange not to see any signs of the risen dead\nhere in the heart of Dagsion.
MID_EV00_012_m01_003: If that's where we are. It feels almost like this place\nis outside the world...
MID_EV00_012_m01_004: <NCA>"What is this place?"
MID_EV00_012_m01_006: 'Tis a special place. I call it the Obelisk Chamber.
MID_EV00_012_m01_008: Only a few people know this chamber exists beneath\nmy temple.
MID_EV00_012_m01_009: It was she who asked me to prepare it, in case\ndisaster ever struck this land.
MID_EV00_012_m01_018: Since I am the Goddess of Fate, I enjoy the power to\nglimpse into the future.
MID_EV00_012_m01_019: And one of my visions showed me a terrible\ndisturbance in the causality of this land.
MID_EV00_012_m01_020: One so awful that it could destroy the world if\nleft unchecked.
MID_EV00_012_m01_021: Since then, I have been searching for powerful\nwarriors to gather together at this moment in time.
MID_EV00_012_m01_022: In the roiling waters of causality, I have found\nwarriors fit to the task.
MID_EV00_012_m01_056: Each possesses staggering power and a noble soul.\nAny one of them is worth a thousand.
MID_EV00_012_m01_057: Let us call them...hmm...the Flame Lords of Dagda.
MID_EV00_012_m01_058: We'll never win the battles ahead without them.\nWe need as many as we can recruit.
MID_EV00_012_m01_023: <NCA>"Where can we find them?"
MID_EV00_012_m01_060: 
MID_EV00_012_m01_024: Alas, they're all dead now. More of Balor's pawns.
MID_EV00_012_m01_025: Come to think of it, you crossed swords with them\nat Alcineus Span.
MID_EV00_012_m01_026: What?! Then this war is lost before it started!
MID_EV00_012_m01_027: Don't look so panicked. I have a plan. You there—\nlisten carefully.
MID_EV00_012_m01_028: The obelisks in this chamber allow you to intervene\nin each warrior's past.
MID_EV00_012_m01_029: We can use these to bend the laws of causality and\nguide the warriors to safety in our present.
MID_EV00_012_m01_042: That's incredible. The sort of help only a goddess\ncan provide.
MID_EV00_012_m01_047: Yes...but even I, the Goddess of Fate, am limited in\nwhat I can do in the past.
MID_EV00_012_m01_048: For example, I can't reverse major events like\nBalor's resurrection.
MID_EV00_012_m01_049: Tweak even the edges of something like that, and\nit will snap back to its original shape with time.
MID_EV00_012_m01_050: <NCA>"I'll do what must be done."
MID_EV00_012_m01_061: <NCB>"Let's get started."
MID_EV00_012_m01_051: Good. Better to act than to fret! Now try touching\none of the obelisks.
MID_EV00_012_m01_054: Don't worry. I'll be there with you on your journey.
MID_EV00_012_m01_059: We wouldn't want you to get lost in the flow of time.